#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:1
msgid "jsesc"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:3
msgid ""
"Given some data, _jsesc_ returns a stringified representation of that "
"data. jsesc is similar to `JSON.stringify()` except:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:5
msgid ""
"it outputs JavaScript instead of JSON [by default](#json), enabling "
"support for data structures like ES6 maps and sets;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:6
msgid "it offers [many options](#api) to customize the output;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:7
msgid ""
"its output is ASCII-safe [by default](#minimal), thanks to its use of "
"[escape sequences](https://mathiasbynens.be/notes/javascript-escapes) "
"where needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:9
msgid ""
"For any input, jsesc generates the shortest possible valid printable-"
"ASCII-only output. [Here’s an online demo.](https://mothereff.in/js-"
"escapes)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:11
msgid ""
"jsesc’s output can be used instead of `JSON.stringify`’s to avoid "
"[mojibake](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mojibake) and other encoding "
"issues, or even to [avoid "
"errors](https://twitter.com/annevk/status/380000829643571200) when "
"passing JSON-formatted data (which may contain U+2028 LINE SEPARATOR, "
"U+2029 PARAGRAPH SEPARATOR, or [lone "
"surrogates](https://esdiscuss.org/topic/code-points-vs-unicode-scalar-"
"values#content-14)) to a JavaScript parser or an UTF-8 encoder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:13
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:15
msgid "Via [npm](https://www.npmjs.com/):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:21
msgid "In [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:27
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:29
msgid "`jsesc(value, options)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:31
msgid ""
"This function takes a value and returns an escaped version of the value "
"where any characters that are not printable ASCII symbols are escaped "
"using the shortest possible (but valid) [escape sequences for use in "
"JavaScript strings](https://mathiasbynens.be/notes/javascript-escapes). "
"The first supported value type is strings:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:41
msgid ""
"Instead of a string, the `value` can also be an array, an object, a map, "
"a set, or a buffer. In such cases, `jsesc` returns a stringified version "
"of the value where any characters that are not printable ASCII symbols "
"are escaped in the same way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:57
msgid ""
"The optional `options` argument accepts an object with the following "
"options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:59
msgid "`quotes`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:61
msgid ""
"The default value for the `quotes` option is `'single'`. This means that "
"any occurrences of `'` in the input string are escaped as `\\'`, so that "
"the output can be used in a string literal wrapped in single quotes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:74
msgid ""
"If you want to use the output as part of a string literal wrapped in "
"double quotes, set the `quotes` option to `'double'`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:84
msgid ""
"If you want to use the output as part of a template literal (i.e. wrapped"
" in backticks), set the `quotes` option to `'backtick'`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:95
msgid "This setting also affects the output for arrays and objects:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:109
msgid "`numbers`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:111
msgid ""
"The default value for the `numbers` option is `'decimal'`. This means "
"that any numeric values are represented using decimal integer literals. "
"Other valid options are `binary`, `octal`, and `hexadecimal`, which "
"result in binary integer literals, octal integer literals, and "
"hexadecimal integer literals, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:135
msgid "`wrap`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:137
msgid ""
"The `wrap` option takes a boolean value (`true` or `false`), and defaults"
" to `false` (disabled). When enabled, the output is a valid JavaScript "
"string literal wrapped in quotes. The type of quotes can be specified "
"through the `quotes` setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:155
msgid "`es6`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:157
msgid ""
"The `es6` option takes a boolean value (`true` or `false`), and defaults "
"to `false` (disabled). When enabled, any astral Unicode symbols in the "
"input are escaped using [ECMAScript 6 Unicode code point escape "
"sequences](https://mathiasbynens.be/notes/javascript-escapes#unicode-"
"code-point) instead of using separate escape sequences for each surrogate"
" half. If backwards compatibility with ES5 environments is a concern, "
"don’t enable this setting. If the `json` setting is enabled, the value "
"for the `es6` setting is ignored (as if it was `false`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:177
msgid "`escapeEverything`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:179
msgid ""
"The `escapeEverything` option takes a boolean value (`true` or `false`), "
"and defaults to `false` (disabled). When enabled, all the symbols in the "
"output are escaped — even printable ASCII symbols."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:189
msgid ""
"This setting also affects the output for string literals within arrays "
"and objects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:191
msgid "`minimal`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:193
msgid ""
"The `minimal` option takes a boolean value (`true` or `false`), and "
"defaults to `false` (disabled). When enabled, only a limited set of "
"symbols in the output are escaped:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:195
msgid "U+0000 `\\0`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:196
msgid "U+0008 `\\b`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:197
msgid "U+0009 `\\t`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:198
msgid "U+000A `\\n`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:199
msgid "U+000C `\\f`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:200
msgid "U+000D `\\r`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:201
msgid "U+005C `\\\\`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:202
msgid "U+2028 `\\u2028`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:203
msgid "U+2029 `\\u2029`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:204
msgid ""
"whatever symbol is being used for wrapping string literals (based on [the"
" `quotes` option](#quotes))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:205
msgid ""
"[lone surrogates](https://esdiscuss.org/topic/code-points-vs-unicode-"
"scalar-values#content-14)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:207
msgid ""
"Note: with this option enabled, jsesc output is no longer guaranteed to "
"be ASCII-safe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:216
msgid "`isScriptContext`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:218
msgid ""
"The `isScriptContext` option takes a boolean value (`true` or `false`), "
"and defaults to `false` (disabled). When enabled, occurrences of "
"[`</script` and `</style`](https://mathiasbynens.be/notes/etago) in the "
"output are escaped as `<\\/script` and `<\\/style`, and "
"[`<!--`](https://mathiasbynens.be/notes/etago#comment-8) is escaped as "
"`\\x3C!--` (or `\\u003C!--` when the `json` option is enabled). This "
"setting is useful when jsesc’s output ends up as part of a `<script>` or "
"`<style>` element in an HTML document."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:227
msgid "`compact`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:229
msgid ""
"The `compact` option takes a boolean value (`true` or `false`), and "
"defaults to `true` (enabled). When enabled, the output for arrays and "
"objects is as compact as possible; it’s not formatted nicely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:248 ../../source/jsesc_README.md:274
msgid "This setting has no effect on the output for strings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:250
msgid "`indent`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:252
msgid ""
"The `indent` option takes a string value, and defaults to `'\\t'`. When "
"the `compact` setting is disabled (`false`), the value of the `indent` "
"option is used to format the output for arrays and objects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:276
msgid "`indentLevel`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:278
msgid ""
"The `indentLevel` option takes a numeric value, and defaults to `0`. It "
"represents the current indentation level, i.e. the number of times the "
"value of [the `indent` option](#indent) is repeated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:294
msgid "`json`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:296
msgid ""
"The `json` option takes a boolean value (`true` or `false`), and defaults"
" to `false` (disabled). When enabled, the output is valid JSON. "
"[Hexadecimal character escape sequences](https://mathiasbynens.be/notes"
"/javascript-escapes#hexadecimal) and [the `\\v` or `\\0` escape "
"sequences](https://mathiasbynens.be/notes/javascript-escapes#single) are "
"not used. Setting `json: true` implies `quotes: 'double', wrap: true, "
"es6: false`, although these values can still be overridden if needed — "
"but in such cases, the output won’t be valid JSON anymore."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:327
msgid ""
"**Note:** Using this option on objects or arrays that contain non-string "
"values relies on `JSON.stringify()`. For legacy environments like IE ≤ 7,"
" use [a `JSON` polyfill](http://bestiejs.github.io/json3/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:329
msgid "`lowercaseHex`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:331
msgid ""
"The `lowercaseHex` option takes a boolean value (`true` or `false`), and "
"defaults to `false` (disabled). When enabled, any alphabetical "
"hexadecimal digits in escape sequences as well as any hexadecimal integer"
" literals (see [the `numbers` option](#numbers)) in the output are in "
"lowercase."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:348
msgid "`jsesc.version`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsesc_README.md:350
msgid "A string representing the semantic version number."
msgstr ""

